WEBVTT

00:00:05.963 --> 00:00:07.656
<v><b>Claire:</b></v> What are we going to do this weekend?

00:00:07.669 --> 00:00:08.237
<v><b>Joe:</b></v> Hey.

00:00:08.416 --> 00:00:09.431
<v><b>All:</b></v> Hey!

00:00:09.998 --> 00:00:12.750
<v><b>Alison:</b></v> I know, let’s go out for dinner on Saturday.

00:00:12.922 --> 00:00:14.805
We can celebrate your birthday, Brett.

00:00:15.134 --> 00:00:17.347
<v><b>Brett:</b></v> Good idea. Where?

00:00:18.053 --> 00:00:21.612
<v><b>Alison:</b></v> Let’s try somewhere new, somewhere we haven’t been to before.

00:00:21.997 --> 00:00:23.463
<v><b>Brett:</b></v> Yeah, that’s a great idea.

00:00:25.317 --> 00:00:29.877
<v><b>Claire:</b></v> How about that Indian restaurant near the station, Curry Up?

00:00:30.683 --> 00:00:32.901
Mmm, good reviews…

00:00:33.094 --> 00:00:33.894
<v><b>Joe:</b></v> Curry Up?

00:00:34.626 --> 00:00:37.358
I’ve been there. It wasn’t very good.

00:00:38.376 --> 00:00:39.067
<v><b>Claire:</b></v> Really?

00:00:40.393 --> 00:00:42.944
OK. Joe says it’s not great.

00:00:44.139 --> 00:00:45.372
What about Chinese then?

00:00:46.056 --> 00:00:48.455
Somebody told me The Great Wall is very good.

00:00:48.629 --> 00:00:51.717
<v><b>Alison:</b></v> Yes, I haven’t been there, but people say it’s great.

00:00:52.410 --> 00:00:53.360
<v><b>Joe:</b></v> The Great Wall?

00:00:53.623 --> 00:00:55.886
I’ve been there. I went last week.

00:00:56.247 --> 00:00:59.477
It is good, but I don’t really want to go again.

00:01:00.756 --> 00:01:05.373
<v><b>Brett:</b></v> Well, there’s a new Thai place, Thai-Chi. It opened up really recently.

00:01:06.065 --> 00:01:07.033
<v><b>Joe:</b></v> Thai Chi?

00:01:07.337 --> 00:01:09.630
I’ve been there, too. I went on Wednesday.

00:01:12.309 --> 00:01:14.133
<v><b>Alison:</b></v> Well, I don’t know.

00:01:14.579 --> 00:01:18.558
Have you been to … Mexican Wave?

00:01:18.582 --> 00:01:19.918
<v><b>Joe:</b></v> Mexican Wave?

00:01:20.295 --> 00:01:21.275
Yes, I have.

00:01:21.521 --> 00:01:22.640
<v><b>Alison:</b></v> When did you go there?

00:01:22.838 --> 00:01:24.018
<v><b>Joe:</b></v> Last month.

00:01:25.140 --> 00:01:26.858
I went for dinner with people from work.

00:01:31.153 --> 00:01:33.775
<v><b>Alison:</b></v> The Acropolis? That Greek place?

00:01:34.135 --> 00:01:35.795
<v><b>Brett:</b></v> I’m sure Joe’s been there!

00:01:37.361 --> 00:01:39.041
<v><b>Joe:</b></v> No, I haven’t.

00:01:41.666 --> 00:01:43.610
But it closed a few months ago.

00:01:43.634 --> 00:01:45.128
<v><b>Brett:</b></v> Oh, this is ridiculous!

00:01:45.261 --> 00:01:47.125
<v><b>Alison:</b></v> OK, Joe, here’s the answer.

00:01:47.345 --> 00:01:48.694
You cook dinner for us!

00:01:49.053 --> 00:01:50.279
<v><b>Joe:</b></v> OK, sure.

00:01:54.609 --> 00:01:56.849
Come on. I can cook.

00:01:57.748 --> 00:02:00.388
<v><b>Claire:</b></v> Yeah – with a microwave.